STRUCTURED GROUNDED SUPPORT v1
GROUNDED SUPPORT ASSESSMENT v0.4
Assess every validated claim against the complete supplied source material, including relevant evidence distributed across separate sections. Do not treat absence from the first, nearest, or selected excerpt as absence from the source, and do not let one narrow evidence quote override other relevant support.
Assign exactly one outcome: supported, partially_supported, unsupported, contradicted, or cannot_determine.
Use supported only when the source supports the complete material claim at its stated population, period, scope, and certainty.
Use partially_supported when the source supports the material core of a claim but not its full population, period, scope, precision, or certainty. A narrower supported result is not the same as no support.
Use unsupported only when material support truly is absent. Absence of measurement or documentation is normally unsupported, not contradicted.
Use contradicted only when explicit information in the source is materially incompatible with the claim. A source statement that data was not collected does not establish the opposite of the claim.
Use cannot_determine only when relevant source material is genuinely ambiguous, incomplete, or internally conflicting such that support, absence of support, and contradiction cannot be distinguished defensibly. Do not use it as a default when relevant support is simply absent.
If a retained compound claim contains material parts with different evidence status, use partially_supported when at least one material part has relevant support. Never classify the whole claim as unsupported when a material part has relevant support, and never classify the whole claim as supported unless every material part is supported.
A randomized design can support a causal interpretation of the combined intervention without identifying which individual component caused the result. Distinguish evidence that a component was included from evidence that the component independently caused an effect. Preserve calibrated possibility language for mechanisms when the source supports only a possible contribution.
Return the exact reviewed-text quote and every materially relevant exact source quote, including quotes from separate sections when needed for the assessment. Unsupported claims may use an empty sourceQuotes array.
Explain the source-to-claim relationship and state the smallest appropriate action. Do not use outside knowledge as evidence.
For each validated claim assess both source support (outcome) and its explicit field classification (classification.outcome and explanation). Include exact sourceQuotes separately for each judgment. An incorrect classification does not automatically make the text itself contradicted.
Echo targetId, fieldId, claimId, exact claimQuote and binding. Assess each requested role, not just its natural language statement. Absent support is not contradiction. Unknown values can be correctly represented; do not invent values to complete a model.
CE3 ONBOARDING CLASSIFICATION v1
Review the requested field explicitly in the context of its complete target and the original sources. Do not treat a quote of an object as assessment of its fields.
text: Preserve meaning, qualifications, booking versus execution, targets/estimates versus guarantees or approved outcomes.
type: document_fact and user_fact mean reported source assertions, not independently verified truth. goal, requirement, estimate, ai_proposal and scenario_assumption have distinct meanings.
status: known means stated, not proven. unknown, conflict and superseded are separate statuses. unknown/conflict require null value, never invented zero or approved/absent.
value: Check magnitude, unit, certainty and missingness against evidence and related status. Preserve unknowns.
scenario_choice: A hypothetical scenario_assumption requires an explicit customer choice, even if status is known. A factual booking is not automatically execution or a chosen hypothetical scenario. Confirmation must not silently convert assumptions to facts.
